DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The above functions are character classification utility functions, for
     use with wide characters (_w_c_h_a_r___t or _w_i_n_t___t) in the locale _l_o_c.  They be‐
     have in the same way as the versions without the _l suffix, but use the
     specified locale rather than the global or per-thread locale.  These
     functions may be implemented as inline functions in <_w_c_t_y_p_e_._h> and as
     functions in the C library.  See the specific manual pages for more in‐
     formation.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     These functions return the same things as their non-locale versions.  If
     the locale is invalid, their behaviors are undefined.

